Do not name threads on mingw

zeromq calls pthread_setname_np() unconditionally in its __MINGW32__ branch,
without consulting the ZMQ_HAVE_PTHREAD_SETNAME_* results its own configure
script computes. The winpthreads shipped with the mingw-w64 in this toolchain
does not declare that function, so the cross-build fails to compile.

Thread names are diagnostic only - nothing reads them back - so leave the
branch empty rather than carrying a probe for it.

--- a/src/thread.cpp
+++ b/src/thread.cpp
@@ -129,9 +129,7 @@

 #elif defined(__MINGW32__)

-    int rc = pthread_setname_np (pthread_self (), _name);
-    if (rc)
-        return;
+    // not declared by the winpthreads in this toolchain; names are diagnostic

 #else

